{
    "background_story": "Rylie was a brilliant and reclusive physicist who had spent her entire career studying the mysteries of dark matter. Her groundbreaking research had led to a series of innovative experiments, but none as ambitious as her latest project: a machine capable of manipulating the fabric of space-time itself. As Rylie worked tirelessly to perfect the device, she began to notice strange occurrences around her. Equipment would malfunction, and strange noises echoed through the laboratory at night. And then, one fateful evening, Rylie activated the machine, only to feel herself being pulled into a vortex of swirling energy. When the dust settled, she was gone, leaving behind only a cryptic message: 'I have achieved the vanishingly small probability of escape.' Her disappearance sparked a frenzy of speculation, with some believing she had unlocked the secrets of the universe, while others thought she had simply vanished into thin air.",
